{"type":"text","timestamp":1787856193698,"sessionID":"ses_fbb7864b8ffeWNQrvbJh2UxeAB","part":{"id":"prt_044887ae1001tl0YNhkHEZBGtc","messageID":"msg_044886de8001Hk5LtpU2xg568F","sessionID":"ses_fbb7864b8ffeWNQrvbJh2UxeAB","type":"text","text":"**Error – Cannot locate the `understand‑anything` plugin**

Phase 0 of the `/understand` workflow requires the **understand‑anything** plugin (the `@understand‑anything/core` package). The script that builds the plugin looks for a directory containing a `package.json` and a `pnpm‑workspace.yaml`. None of the usual locations (e.g., `$HOME/.understand‑anything-plugin`, `~/understand‑anything/understand‑anything‑plugin`, the skill’s own directory, or any of the Copilot/Opencode fallback paths) contain such a package.

**What to do**

1. **Install the plugin** (Node ≥ 22, pnpm ≥ 10):
   ```bash
   # example installation location
   mkdir -p $HOME/.understand-anything-plugin
   cd $HOME/.understand-anything-plugin
   git clone https://github.com/understand-anything/understand-anything-plugin.git .
   pnpm install   # or npm install if pnpm isn’t available
   pnpm --filter @understand-anything/core build
   ```

2. **Set the environment variable** `CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT` (or any of the fallback variables) to point at the plugin root directory, e.g.:
   ```bash
   export CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT=$HOME/.understand-anything-plugin
   ```

3. **Re‑run the command**:
   ```
   /understand
   ```

Once the plugin is installed and the `CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT` (or one of the alternative paths) points to its root, the `/understand` skill will be able to proceed through all phases and generate the `knowledge-graph.json` file.","time":{"start":1787856190177,"end":1787856193689}}}
